  "text": "I'll start by reading the ego-browser skill and the job inputs so I can transport the approved prompt to grok.com without writing the plan myself.I'll inspect the job folder, approved input, and the wait/clipboard helpers next so the browser run stays inside this lane.I'll read the job metadata and the start of `input.md` so the Korean prompt matches the attachment without rewriting the plan.I'll open a unique task space and inspect grok.com so I can pick the highest available reasoning mode before uploading.The first snapshot was too sparse, so I’ll wait for grok.com to finish loading and inspect the actual composer UI.There's a promo dialog over the composer. I'll dismiss it, then open the model picker and record the highest reasoning mode on this account.The composer is clear. Next I’ll open the model picker and choose the highest reasoning option this account actually shows.The highest reasoning option on this account is **헤비**. I’ll select it, then attach `input.md` and send the Korean request once.Heavy is paywalled on this account, so I’ll close the upgrade dialog and keep **전문가**, the highest reasoning mode already available.Mode is **전문가**. I’ll attach `input.md`, then type the Korean request and send it once.`input.md` is attached. I’ll type the Korean request, send it once, and save the receipt immediately.Prompt and attachment are ready. I’ll send once, then write the submitted receipt with the conversation URL.The request is in. I’ll save the submitted receipt now, then lock in the stop and response selectors before waiting.Receipt is saved. I’ll inspect the live DOM next so the wait helper uses the actual stop and response selectors.Selectors are confirmed. I’ll start the 15-minute wait helper so it can poll until the response is stable.The first wait poll failed immediately. I’ll inspect the helper logs and retry with the same task space.The wait helper’s poll script may be misquoted. I’ll reproduce it exactly and check whether nested ego-browser is being blocked.The poll script works; the first wait likely raced. I’ll start the 15-minute helper again.The wait helper still fails immediately. I’ll inspect its spawned poll process and the browser wrapper next.The poll is landing on stderr, which the wait helper does not read. I’ll inspect the spawn path and see if that can be corrected without changing the helper.The guard wrapper is on PATH later than the real binary. I’ll read it to see how the wait helper is supposed to receive poll output.I’ll send a compact poll through the guard and check whether `FIREFLY_STATE` lands on stdout or stderr.The stop control is gone and a full-looking answer is on the page. I’ll wait 40 seconds and poll again to confirm the text is stable before copying.The answer is stable. I’ll locate the response Copy control, then capture it through the clipboard helper.Copy control is `응답 복사`. I’ll capture the response with the clipboard helper, using the title and ending sentence as anchors.Clipboard capture succeeded. I’ll save the completion snapshot and receipt, then close the task space.Capture is verified. I’ll write the snapshot and completed receipt, then close the task space.Capture is verified. I’ll write the snapshot and completed receipt, then close the task space.Capture is on disk. I’ll close task space 5 now, without keeping the browser session.Transport finished. grok.com returned a complete nine-section plan; it was copied with the on-page Copy control and saved without rewriting.\n\n**Result:** complete  \n**Mode used:** 전문가 (깊게 생각 · Grok 4.6). 헤비 was visible but opened a SuperGrok Heavy paywall; the paid plan was not changed.  \n**Conversation:** https://grok.com/c/79ba3f47-3053-4be3-936c-296d79b5e707  \n**Output:** `plan.md` (30,212 bytes, SHA256 `692a682d41f3f1c08ac5781234182929cc813be14155809bf006375f800b0953`)  \n**Extraction:** `ego-copy+os-pbpaste` via `button[aria-label=\"응답 복사\"]`  \n**Receipt:** `web-receipt.json`  \n**Task space:** 5, closed (`keep: f